<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 May, from 1110 to 1981.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1110">1110 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">916 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baldwin I of Jerusalem captures Beirut from the Fatimids</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege begun in February, the forces of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem">Baldwin I of Jerusalem</a> took the coastal city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beirut">Beirut</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>, with the help of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrand-of-toulouse">Bertrand of Toulouse</a> and a Genoese fleet.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-jerusalem">Baldwin I of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1344">1344 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">682 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Latin Christian league defeats a Turkish fleet at Pallene</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Smyrniote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusades</a>, the fleet of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Christian league defeated Turkish raiders at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallene">Pallene</a> Peninsula in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>. The crusades, sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-vi">Pope Clement VI</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">Beylik</a> of Aydin, were mostly successful in restricting piracy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Christendom</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1568">1568 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">458 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary, Queen of Scots is defeated at Langside</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mary's forces were routed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a> by the regent Moray. Three days later she fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> kept her captive for nineteen years before her execution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1619">1619 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">407 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Johan van Oldenbarnevelt is executed in The Hague</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-van-oldenbarnevelt">Johan van Oldenbarnevelt</a>, Land's Advocate of Holland and the leading statesman of the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>, was beheaded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a> after his conviction for treason. He had clashed with Stadtholder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-prince-of-orange">Maurice of Nassau</a> amid the conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/remonstrants">Remonstrants</a> and Counter-Remonstrants.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johan-van-oldenbarnevelt">Johan van Oldenbarnevelt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1787">1787 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The First Fleet sails from Portsmouth for Australia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eleven ships under Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-phillip">Arthur Phillip</a> left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> carrying some 1,400 people, about half of them convicts. They reached Botany Bay in January 1788 and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1846">1846 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">180 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Congress declares war on Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress approved President Polk's request for war after clashes near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a>. By the 1848 peace, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> had ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> and most of the present American Southwest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Churchill offers 'blood, toil, tears and sweat'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his first speech to the Commons as Prime Minister, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> promised a long struggle and declared his aim to be 'victory at all costs'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1981">1981 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John Paul II is shot in St Peter's Square</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Mehmet Ali</a> Ağca shot and seriously wounded the Pope as he greeted crowds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. John Paul II recovered and later visited his attacker in prison to forgive him.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 May <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maria-theresa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maria Theresa</span><span class="tp">1717–1780</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-ix"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-ix.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Pius IX</span><span class="tp">1792–1878</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-tolbert"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-tolbert.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Tolbert</span><span class="tp">1913–1980</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 13 May <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/takeda-shingen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Takeda Shingen</span><span class="tp">1521–1573</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johan-van-oldenbarnevelt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johan-van-oldenbarnevelt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johan van Oldenbarnevelt</span><span class="tp">1547–1619</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/apolinario-mabini"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/apolinario-mabini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Apolinario Mabini</span><span class="tp">1864–1903</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/khalifa-bin-zayed-al-nahyan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/khalifa-bin-zayed-al-nahyan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Khalifa bin Zayed Al Nahyan</span><span class="tp">1948–2022</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alice-munro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alice-munro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alice Munro</span><span class="tp">1931–2024</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-mujica"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-mujica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Mujica</span><span class="tp">1935–2025</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
